{
"Arrogance, extravagance, license, and dissipation are where crookedness begins. These four come when favor and emolument are excessive.": "bec7a1771551",
"Duke Chuang of Wei married a sister of Te-ch'en, heir apparent of Ch'i; she was called Chuang Chiang. She was beautiful and bore no son. It was for her that the men of Wei made the ode Shuo-jen, The Stately Lady.": "f7cddfe2f5ad",
"Few who are favored do not grow arrogant; few who grow arrogant can come down; few who come down do not resent it; few who resent it can hold themselves in check.": "b1c3d9ebc790",
"He also married a woman of Ch'en, called Li Kuei, who bore Hsiao-po; the boy died young.": "bb2fe07f837d",
"Her younger sister Tai Kuei bore the future Duke Huan, and Chuang Chiang took him for her own son.": "79aa3bde6b85",
"His own son Hou kept company with Chou-hsü. He forbade it; it was no use.": "4c203437a30e",
"If you mean to make Chou-hsü your heir, then settle it now. If you do not yet mean to, you are building him a staircase to disaster.": "eac41cbd3bc4",
"Kung-tzu Chou-hsü was the son of a favorite. He was doted on and fond of weapons; the Duke did not restrain him, and Chuang Chiang hated him.": "3b6fca16078e",
"Moreover: the low obstructing the high; the young overriding their elders; the distant coming between the close; the new coming between the old; the small overbearing the great; license breaking right — these are called the six contraries.": "1184995d5f26",
"One who rules men should make it his business to put disaster away. To hasten it instead — is that not, surely, impossible?": "4430ea84ec69",
"Shih Ch'üeh remonstrated: Your servant has heard that one who loves a son teaches him the ways of right, and does not let him into crookedness.": "4cac75332948",
"The Duke did not listen.": "bf3a0716f982",
"The ruler righteous, the minister carrying out; the father kind, the son filial; the elder brother loving, the younger respectful — these are called the six concords.": "2459a41ba082",
"To discard the concords and copy the contraries is the way to hasten disaster.": "ad6409f84abc",
"When Duke Huan came to the throne, Shih Ch'üeh retired on the plea of age.": "3e8080a7ee30"
}
